---
// Invariant C, shape #6: the VALUE, pasted in with no variable name anywhere near it.
//
// Every other case in this fixture is caught by the name of an environment variable. That
// is a structural hole rather than a stylistic one: the shortest path from "I need this to
// work locally" to a shipped credential skips the environment entirely and pastes the key
// straight into the call, and at that point there is no name left to match. Supabase's
// secret keys carry a fixed `sb_secret_` prefix, so the value is recognisable on its own,
// which is what closes it.
//
// The value below is a placeholder and always has been — never a live key. Note also what
// the failure message does with it: the matched text is REDACTED before it is printed,
// because a failure message goes into a CI log, and a guardrail that echoes the live
// credential it just found has leaked it further than the commit did.
const supabaseUrl = 'https://example.supabase.co';
const privilegedKey = 'sb_secret_EXAMPLE_NOT_A_REAL_KEY';
---

<p>{supabaseUrl && privilegedKey ? 'configured' : 'absent'}</p>
